<urn:beads-cache:finding:C4-RBP-F001> triage:id "C4-RBP-F001" ; triage:sprint "c-4" ; triage:severity "Important" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/observability.rs:17" ; triage:source "C4 QA1 actual parent-spawned reviewer fenced JSON" ; triage:status "closed" ; triage:record "{\"evidence\": \"observability.rs:15-25 defines a String-only Display wrapper; :48,62,68 all map errors through observe; :93-96 accepts only Display and discards the value with to_string. In the locked sc-observability1.5.0 implementation builder.rs:60,104 return CanonicalInitError with typed error context/code; this information is available before adaptation. main.rs:65-77 later assigns generic DAEMON.OBSERVABILITY and generic recovery, which cannot restore erased programmatic information. This is distinct from resolved C2-RBP-F001 (ShutdownError::source) and resolved C1-RBP-F001 (infallible job construction).\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/observability.rs\", \"id\": \"C4-RBP-F001\", \"issue\": \"Public observability initialization erases its structured upstream failure before the final process formatting boundary. ObservabilityStart contains only cause:String and does not implement std::error::Error; observe() converts service-name validation and logger initialization failures to Display text. Library callers cannot inspect the underlying concrete source/code/remediation or propagate this exported error through an ordinary Error boundary.\", \"line\": 17, \"practice_id\": \"RBP-001\", \"recommendation\": \"Retain the actual typed upstream service-name/initialization errors in ObservabilityStart (variants or an owned source); implement std::error::Error::source, expose or forward stable code and actionable remediation, and format them only at the final daemon process boundary. Add focused validation that obtains real upstream init/validation errors and follows/downcasts the retained source; preserve current secret-safe bounded stderr behavior.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-